    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d349">

                <pb facs="0405" n="1239" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1239"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 658.119/399</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Laughlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-29T17:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 29, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 8.22 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>10324. War Trade Board [from Sheldon]:</p>
                <p>No. 675. The Swedish agreement was signed this afternoon subject to ratification
                    which Swedish delegates state is only matter of form as their Government has not
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">now?</hi>] seen full text. Will cable you a summary
                    of some of the important changes in the draft agreement which was sent you on
                    May 21, as well as summary of covering letters exchanged. Do not publish
                    contents until further advised but no harm in announcing that agreement has been
                    signed. Please notify Shipping Board.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Laughlin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
